            <ArticleTitle>Graft aneurysm complicating an extracranial-intracranial bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>548-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/02688690902919151</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a patient that developed an aneurysm on a grafted saphenous vein following an extracranial-intracranial (EC-IC) bypass. Although saphenous vein graft aneurysms (SVGAs) have been described as a rare complication following coronary surgery, we are unaware of any previously reported cases of SVGAs following EC-IC bypass.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
